---
layout: default
---
<div class="post archive-page">
  <header class="post-header">
    {% if page.type == 'categories' %}
      <h1 class="post-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-tag fa-sm"></i> {{ page.title }}</h1>
      <p class="post-description">このカテゴリの記事一覧</p>
    {% elsif page.type == 'year' %}
      <h1 class="post-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-calendar fa-sm"></i> {{ page.date | date: '%Y' }}年</h1>
      <p class="post-description">この年の記事一覧</p>
    {% elsif page.type == 'tags' %}
      <h1 class="post-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-hashtag fa-sm"></i> {{ page.title }}</h1>
      <p class="post-description">このタグが付いた記事一覧</p>
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  <article class="archive">
    <ul class="archive-list">
      {% comment %}
        Upstream tests the redirect with an `== blank` comparison. page.documents
        yields Jekyll document drops, on which a missing key returns Ruby nil,
        and nil does not compare equal to Liquid's `blank` literal -- so that
        test is false for every post without a redirect, the else branch runs,
        and piping nil through relative_url renders href="". That left every
        link on every archive page empty. Testing truthiness instead (the same
        idiom _pages/blog.md already uses) is what actually works.
      {% endcomment %}
      {% for document in page.documents %}
        <li>
          <time datetime="{{ document.date | date_to_xmlschema }}">{{ document.date | date: '%Y年%-m月%-d日' }}</time>
          {% if document.redirect %}
            {% if document.redirect contains '://' %}
              <a class="post-link" href="{{ document.redirect }}" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener">{{ document.title }}</a>
            {% else %}
              <a class="post-link" href="{{ document.redirect | relative_url }}">{{ document.title }}</a>
            {% endif %}
          {% else %}
            <a class="post-link" href="{{ document.url | relative_url }}">{{ document.title }}</a>
          {% endif %}
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </article>
</div>
